{
  "id": "mullerian-mimicry",
  "term": "Müllerian mimicry",
  "definition": "Müllerian mimicry is a mutual form of resemblance in which unpalatable, warning-signaled species evolve similar appearances, so their shared pattern is linked with reciprocal selective pressure and coevolution. In the source example, two butterfly species show parallel warning coloration and repeated codivergence consistent with this process.",
